# Review routing.
#
# NOT YET ACTIVE: the @direwolf-project organisation and its teams do not exist
# while the repository is private and single-author. GitHub silently ignores an
# entry naming a team it cannot resolve, so do not read a green PR as evidence
# that a security reviewer saw it. The rules in CONTRIBUTING.md
# ("Security-sensitive changes") are the authority; this file mechanises them
# once the org exists, and creating those teams is a precondition for making
# the repository public.

# The trusted computing base. Every change here is security-relevant by
# definition (ADR-0018, ADR-0019).
/crates/dwkd-authority/   @direwolf-project/security
/crates/dwkd-broker/      @direwolf-project/security

# The wire format between the cognition plane and the authority plane. A new
# DWKP operation needs a written argument that it is not a second path from
# cognition to effect (docs/adr/README.md, rule 5).
/schemas/                 @direwolf-project/security
# The crate that defines that wire, and that both daemons link (ADR-0033). Its
# dependency closure is the authority's from M3.
/crates/dwk-proto/        @direwolf-project/security
# The generators, and the hand-written Python wire layer they target: a change
# to either changes what the runtime accepts without touching a schema.
/tools/protogen/          @direwolf-project/security
/scripts/gen_proto_python.py @direwolf-project/security
/runtime/src/direwolf/wire/  @direwolf-project/security
/tests/protocol/vectors/  @direwolf-project/security

# Architecture decisions are immutable once accepted; a change here is either a
# new record or a mistake.
/docs/adr/                @direwolf-project/architecture

# The boundary rules themselves, and the supply-chain policy.
/architecture.toml        @direwolf-project/security
/deny.toml                @direwolf-project/security
/Cargo.lock               @direwolf-project/security

# CI has no secrets and a read-only token today. Keeping it that way is a
# review matter, because the first `permissions: write` is the one nobody
# notices.
/.github/                 @direwolf-project/security
